.TH FORK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fork \- create a child process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B "pid_t fork(void);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a child process using the Linux fork syscall. The child has a separate
address space and inherits open descriptors referring to the same open file
descriptions as the parent.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the child PID in the parent and 0 in the child. On failure it returns
\-1 in the parent, sets
.BR errno ,
and creates no child. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.B EAGAIN
and
.BR ENOMEM .
Other Linux fork errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Crunch provides no atfork handlers. The parent must reap the child separately;
this interface does not provide a wait function. Crunch errno is process\-wide
within each process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getpid (3crunch),
.BR kill (3crunch),
.BR fork (2),
.BR waitpid (2)
